<Layout title="Old craft. New conversations. — The Gubbi">
<header class="philosophy-hero wrap"><h1>Serious about craft.<br/><span class="serif">Less so about ourselves.</span></h1><p>A few things we want every Gubbi object to stand for.</p></header>
<section class="principles wrap"><article><span>THE SUBJECT</span><h2>Specific is <span class="serif">special.</span></h2><p>“Nice object” is fine. “That is literally you” is better. We start with a recognisable feeling, a local ritual, or a joke that has lived rent-free in our heads for far too long.</p></article><article><span>THE MATERIAL</span><h2>Let wood <span class="serif">be wood.</span></h2><p>Our starting point is Channapatna’s turned-wood craft. The final shapes need to work with the maker and the material. A concept is an invitation to prototype, not a promise to manufacture the impossible.</p></article><article><span>THE INTENTION</span><h2>Keep it <span class="serif">around.</span></h2><p>We want things you move from one desk to the next. Objects with a story you remember, a surface you want to touch, and a place in the room long after the joke first lands.</p></article><article><span>THE PROMISE</span><h2>Show the <span class="serif">real thing.</span></h2><p>Real makers. Real materials. Real product photographs. We’re not there yet, and we’ll say so. The collection you see today is a preview of where we’re headed.</p></article></section>
<section class="craft-interlude"><div class="wrap"><ProductCrop position="p-4" alt="Workflow Spinner 2AM, turned wood and colour in a playful object concept"/><div><h2>Old hands.<br/>New <span class="serif">mischief.</span></h2><p>The ambition is a collaboration: contemporary ideas shaped by people who understand the craft. Production partners and process stories will appear here as the first batch takes shape.</p><a href="/shop" class="button button--light">Explore the concepts <Icon/></a></div></div></section>
<section class="nest-note wrap"><img src="/brand/gubbi-flower.svg" alt="" width="100" height="100"/><div><h2>A little room for <span class="serif">the sparrow.</span></h2><p>Our plan is for every object sold to help put up a sparrow nest box in Bengaluru. We’ll publish the partner, the process and the evidence before making that promise part of a purchase. No counter until there’s something real to count.</p><a href="/story" class="text-link">Why the sparrow matters to us <Icon/></a></div></section>
</Layout>
